User labels (h89s): free-text tags on a todo, distinct from the plugin's display **type**. They
ride their own observed-remove OR-set, so re-adding the same label still leaves one, and a remove
only detaches what it observed. Filter the list with `--label`.

Set up a workspace and create a todo to label:

```console
$ nxf init --plugin personal-todo --json
[..]

```

```console
$ nxf create --type todo --title "Book venue" --description "Reserve the event space" --priority soon --json
[..]

```

Attach two labels (idempotent), then list them — sorted and de-duplicated:

```console
$ nxf label add ab12.0001 errands --json
{"msg":"ab12.0001 labelled errands","ok":true}

```

```console
$ nxf label add ab12.0001 home --json
{"msg":"ab12.0001 labelled home","ok":true}

```

```console
$ nxf label list ab12.0001 --json
["errands","home"]

```

Filter the list to a label (only the labelled todo is returned):

```console
$ nxf list --label errands --json
[..]

```

Detach one label (observed-remove); the other remains:

```console
$ nxf label remove ab12.0001 errands --json
{"msg":"ab12.0001 unlabelled errands","ok":true}

```

```console
$ nxf label list ab12.0001 --json
["home"]

```
